      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$, we need to find the inverse $f^{-1}$.\n\nWe use the property of function composition that states:\n\n$(f \\circ g \\circ h)(x) = f(g(h(x)))$\n\nTaking the inverse of $f$, we get:\n\n$(f^{-1}) = h^{-1} \\circ g^{-1} \\circ f^{-1}$\n\nLet's apply this to $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$ by setting $h = p$, $g = q$, and $f = r$. We thus have:\n\n$(f^{-1}) = r^{-1} \\circ q^{-1} \\circ p^{-1}$\n\nThe given choice matches this expression. Thus, for $f = q \\circ p \\circ r$, the correct expression is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{A}\\]",
