      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the inverse of the composite function \\( f = q \\circ p \\circ r \\), we need to determine the order of the inverse functions. We start by recalling the property of inverse functions: if \\( f \\) is invertible, then the inverse \\( f^{-1} \\) is also invertible, and the order in which we apply the inverse functions is reversed.\n\nThe general rule is:\n\\[\n(f \\circ g \\circ h)^{-1} = h^{-1} \\circ g^{-1} \\circ f^{-1}\n\\]\nIn our case, \\( f = q \\circ p \\circ r \\), so applying the rule for inverse functions, we need to find \\( (q \\circ p \\circ r)^{-1} \\):\n\\[\n(q \\circ p \\circ r)^{-1} = r^{-1} \\circ p^{-1} \\circ q^{-1}\n\\]\nThis matches option C. Therefore, the inverse of the composite function is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{C}\n\\]",
